  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Carousel – the ball round the goal and two in the slot",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. Four spots: A at the centre line by the right boards with the balls, B in the right corner, C in the left corner and D at the centre line by the left boards. A passes along the boards to B and heads straight for the slot. B carries the ball behind the goal, passes on to C and comes out in front of goal on their own side. C plays up the boards to D, who has two players to choose from in front of goal and passes to the one who is freest. The receiver shoots first time.\n\nRotation: everyone moves one spot in the direction of the ball (A to B, B to C, C to D and D to the A line). Switch sides after a few minutes so the ball goes round the goal the other way.\n\nVariant: a defender steps in front of goal and can only cover one of the two – D reads who is free. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep the ball moving round the goal without stopping – that is what pulls the defence apart."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A and B: spread out in front of goal so one defender cannot cover both."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "D: look up before the ball arrives and decide early who gets the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The shooter keeps the stick on the floor and shoots first time."
    }
  ],
